  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Light to occasionally moderate rain is likely tonight into \nThursday with scattered thunderstorms possible in Northern Maine \nThursday afternoon. Little to no drought relief expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION... Intermittent light rain \noverspreads much of the north tonight, with a band of rain also \ndeveloping further south toward Bangor/Downeast Thursday \nmorning. As the cold front moves through from west to east \nThursday afternoon, there is the potential for some convection \njust ahead of the front, mainly over the north. Model soundings \nshow some weak instability up to 500 J/kg which could produce \nsome thunder. Low freezing levels around 7500 ft may favor some \nsmall hail with any storms. Overall, not expecting any severe \nstorms. The potential for drought relief is relatively low as \ntotal precipitation is expected to be generally below 0.50 \ninches, with the highest amounts over the north. That said, rain\ntotals are trending a bit higher, and one tenth to one quarter \ninch is now possible Downeast as well. Rain ends Thursday night.",
